                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "SG/ZH: School Girl/Zombie Hunter Review (Steam Deck OLED 1TB)\n\nIf you're looking for a quirky, action-packed zombie game with plenty of anime charm, SG/ZH: School Girl/Zombie Hunter is a surprisingly fun experience! Taking control of five schoolgirls trapped in a zombie-infested city, the game delivers fast-paced combat, over-the-top action, and plenty of chaotic moments as you blast through hordes of the undead.\n\nWhat makes the game enjoyable is its simple pick-up-and-play gameplay. The missions are straightforward, the weapon variety keeps things interesting, and mowing down waves of zombies never gets old. While the story isn't trying to reinvent the genre, it embraces its B-movie style and keeps the adventure entertaining from start to finish.\n\nI played this entirely on a Steam Deck OLED 1TB, and the experience was excellent. Performance was smooth, controls felt comfortable on the Deck, and the game's mission-based structure made it perfect for both short and extended play sessions. The OLED screen also helps the colorful anime visuals and effects pop nicely during gameplay.\n\nOverall, SG/ZH: School Girl/Zombie Hunter is a fun hidden gem for fans of anime-style action games and zombie shooters. It may not be the deepest game out there, but its charm, satisfying combat, and portable-friendly gameplay make it an easy recommendation, especially on the Steam Deck OLED.\n\nScore: 8/10\n Fun zombie-slaying action, great portability on Steam Deck, and plenty of cheesy anime goodness.",
